README for asioemu

* Introduction
The program has been written in order to copy Atari 8-bit disks to
ATR images on a PC. For this purpose the software emulates the behavior
of an Atari SIO disk drive.

    ------------
    |  ATARI   |           
    | Computer |
    ------------
         |
   --------------           --------------
   |   ATARI    |           |  asioemu   |
   | Disk drive |---------- | Disk drive | 
   |     1      |           |     2      |
   --------------           --------------

On the Atari computer any standard copy software can be used.

* SIO connection
The Atari SIO port is connected to a PC UART. Because of different
operation volatge (12V PC UART vs 5V Atari SIO), SIO and UART MUST NOT
be connected without voltage level shifting. For details on how
to connect, please check MAX232 and SIO2PC on the internet.

asioemu needs the "data in" (SIO pin 3) and "data out" (SIO pin 5) 
information only. The "command" (SIO pin 7) line is not required. This 
approach should make  the software very flexible  regarding supported 
hardware.
